   "evidence": "Read of the file: `@[simp]` appears on `bilinMap_update_add`, `bilinMap_pair_smul_snd`, `bilinMap_pair_add_snd`, `bilinMap_pair_sub_snd`, `neg_bilinMap`, `bilinMap_pair_neg_snd`, but not on `bilinMap_update_smul`, `bilinMap_update_neg`, `bilinMap_update_sub`. The module docstring (lines 33-36) presents all six `_smul`/`_add`/`_sub` lemmas as one group, \"it is linear in each fixed vector\".",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Mathematics/LinearAlgebra/Alternating/BilinMap.lean",
   "fix": "Make the family uniform. Mathlib's analogues `Matrix.det_updateRow_add` and `det_updateRow_smul` (Mathlib/LinearAlgebra/Matrix/Determinant/Basic.lean:388, 397) are both plain theorems, and the `_update_*` lemmas here exist only to drive the `_pair_*_snd` versions, so dropping `@[simp]` from `bilinMap_update_add` is the smaller change; alternatively add `@[simp]` to all four.",
   "issue": "`bilinMap_update_add` is `@[simp]` while its three siblings in the same advertised family are not: `bilinMap_update_smul` (line 88), `bilinMap_update_neg` (line 151), `bilinMap_update_sub` (line 172). `simp` will push an `add` out through `Function.update` but leave `smul`, `sub` and `neg` in place, so a term like `f.bilinMap (Function.update m i (a \u2022 x - y))` is left half-normalized.",
   "line": 98
  }
 ],
